Problem Statement

Background & Context

Modern digital platforms process millions of user-generated posts, comments, and media items daily. Maintaining platform integrity requires enforcing community guidelines against hate speech, harassment, misinformation, spam, and copyright violations.

Core Challenge

• High False Positive Rates: Overly aggressive automated AI moderation systems frequently remove benign user content. This triggers user backlash, high appeal volumes, and a loss of trust.
• Operational Queue Bottlenecks: Human moderation teams face inconsistent review SLA (Service Level Agreement) times when processing flagged user reports, leading to delayed enforcement on harmful content.
• Lack of Executive Transparency: Trust & Safety leadership lacks real-time, unified visibility into policy violation trends, classifier accuracy, and appeal overturn ratios to fine-tune AI moderation thresholds.

Proposed Solution

Build an enterprise-grade Trust & Safety Analytics & Policy Intelligence Dashboard that aggregates moderation telemetry to monitor AI vs. human decision accuracy, track review SLAs, and quantify appeal overturn rates for platform fairness.
